    "chunk_size_bytes": 1511,
    "chunk_text": "Let me say something uncomfortable. A democracy only works when voters are intelligent enough to choose leaders of character. Sri Lanka has proven, year after year, that we are not there yet. Without hatred, without malice, I state the obvious: we have given birth to a state that is extremely low and despicable. Not because of one man or one party, but because millions of us refused to think.\n\nI see a government changing the Buddha\u2019s birthday. I see a majority losing their wisdom. I see monks silent when they should roar. I see lay people arguing about cricket while their Dhamma island sinks.\n\nBut I also hope. I hope because the Dhamma is not a calendar date. The Dhamma is a living truth. No government can erase it \u2014 though they can certainly insult it. And insults can wake us up.\n\nDo not share this article out of anger. Share it out of awareness. Check the calendar yourself. Ask your local monk: When is the real Vesak? Ask your Member of Parliament: Why are you silent? And ask yourself: What kind of Buddhist am I, if I allow politicians to rewrite the birth of my Lord Buddha?\n\nLet us not wait for next year. Let us not wait for lanterns and pandals to return. Let this silent Vesak be the loudest wakeup call in our history.\n\nMay the Triple Gem protect us \u2014 from ourselves. Yours in the Dhamma,\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
