    "language": "en",
    "md5": "cefce5f0916993d42685f98af226b737",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1471,
    "chunk_text": "\u2018The connoisseur needs to make an effort and have the necessary interest in order to appreciate a work of art. There should be space and opportunity for anyone to appreciate art in accordance with his or her knowledge and understanding. It is unlikely that everyone could read any of this in the very same way.\u2019\n\nIt is for this reason that some declare that they do not understand H A Karunaratne\u2019s work. They offer as an excuse the fact that they have not obtained any formal education on the relevant subject. Armed with such an excuse they do even try to appreciate art. It\u2019s the same in the universities and in society in general. And yet, based on whatever knowledge they may have acquired on some other unrelated, subject, they take decisions on the administering of subtle art forms they are clueless about. Therefore it is important to discuss why artists like H A Karunaratne worked in isolation.\n\nThere are of course some who mimicked him and even claimed that they too could produce similar work. That they floundered is quite apparent when their work is examined.\n\nSo, in this context, one could ask if even his formal students truly understood his teaching techniques. He would penetrate the creation at some point and through it delve into the canvas. The experience obtained in this journey would give him the strength to clear the pathways ahead. This is not easy to understand. It is hard to travel along that path. It is in fact an arduous path."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-05-02-islandlk-3c3a496b",
