    "md5": "0845aac5e8900cb38c61ecd62d908aec",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2021,
    "chunk_text": "Our scene for Top Model of the World 2026\n\nNetalie Withanage is new to our modelling scene but she is already in the spotlight \u2026 in an awesome way. Yes, she has been selected to represent Sri Lanka at the Top Model of the World pageant and she is all excited to a part of this happening.\n\nIn fact, the exciting scene for Netalie began in March, this year, when she took top honours at the Colombo Fashion Week \u2018New Face\u2019 audition.\n\nA couple of weeks later, under the guidance of Brian Kerkoven, she found herself on the ramp at the prestigious Colombo Fashion Week event, held from 01to 04 April.\n\nThe 19-year-old dark tan Fashion Model, who stands 5ft 8 inches in height, loves reading, and anything connected with literature.\n\nShe studied at the Seventh-Day Adventist High School in Kandana and excelled in English, winning several school prizes, we well.\n\nHaving now come into the spotlight, as a model, Netalie says she is keen to get fully involved in this scene.\n\nOf course, she has the potential to excel at the Top Model of the World pageant and is working hard at achieving her goal.\n\nFounded in Miami, in 1993, Top Model of the World is run by the World Beauty Organisation and focuses on professional modelling careers \u2014 runway skills, photographic presence, and industry potential \u2014 not just beauty. It\u2019s billed as the world\u2019s largest international modelling contest.\n\nThis year\u2019s contest is being held in Sahl Hasheesh, near Hurghada, Egypt, at the V Luxury Resort, with the grand finale at THE ARENA on 08 June, 2026.\n\nEgypt is hosting it again after a successful 31st anniversary edition in Hurghada.\n\nPrevious finals have been held in Shanghai, Berlin, Miami, Hong Kong, Sharm El Sheikh and Cairo.\n\nAround 40 elite models, from around the globe, will be competing, this year, and the programme includes professional photoshoots and video shoots with Egypt\u2019s top photographers, plus art videographers from Germany.\n\nThe content goes into the models\u2019 portfolios for real career building."
